        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.656,
            0.713,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12.9 What Are the Benefits of an Ecosystem?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.696,
            0.744,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have learnt that biotic components and abiotic components of an ecosystem depend on each other and support various life processes. Humans also benefit from ecosystems. For example, forests provide fresh air, fertile soil, food, fibres, timber, and medicines. Similarly, aquatic ecosystems provide water and food. Ecosystems also offer aesthetic and recreational value. These support our well-being and shows how closely nature and humans are connected. However, when we overuse or misuse natural resources, we disturb the balance in nature."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.865,
            0.743,
            0.903
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now let us look at a real-life example of a threatened ecosystem — the Sundarbans."
            }
          ]
        },
